course: dictionary
lesson: 8796
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning the writer wants. The word shark can mean a large fish, but it can also mean a person who cheats others. «Hammerhead sharks have wide heads with an eye at each end, and they swing their heads from side to side as they search.» Wide heads, eyes and searching tell you this is the fish.
explain: Now read this: a loan shark lends people money and then cheats them. The word loan is the clue. A loan is money lent to someone, so a loan shark must be a person, not a fish. Check by putting your meaning in the sentence: a fish that cheats people does not make sense, so you know the person meaning is right.
explain: Look at the sentences about sharks and people too. «Sharks very rarely bite people; people are not their normal food» tells you a shark bite is not common. Rarely means not often. Always ask what word would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: Shark (noun) means a large fish with a long body, fins, rows of sharp teeth and a skeleton made of cartilage instead of bone.
fact: Informally, a shark is also a person who cheats others out of money, as in loan shark.
fact: Sharks breathe with gills and keep losing their teeth and growing new ones.
fact: «Megalodon» was a giant shark, perhaps 15 to 20 metres long, that died out about 3.6 million years ago.
fact: Context clues, like loan or fins, help you tell which meaning of a word the writer means.
exercise: «Hammerhead sharks have wide heads with an eye at each end.» What is a shark in this sentence? | A loud noise | A kind of boat | *A large fish | A person who cheats others
exercise: Sam reads that a loan shark is a person. Which clue shows this? | *Loan, which is about money | Fish | Teeth | Sea
exercise: Which word from «Sharks very rarely bite people» means not often? | People | Bite | *Rarely | Sharks
test: «Megalodon was a giant shark, perhaps 15 to 20 metres long.» What does giant mean here? | Very slow | Very dark | Very small | *Very large
test: What is a shark's skeleton made of? | Shell | *Cartilage | Wood | Bone
exam: Which sentence uses shark to mean a person? | Megalodon was a giant shark | Sharks have rows of sharp teeth | *A loan shark cheated the man out of his savings | Walking sharks can survive for hours
